-- title:
--   Base change of a smooth-point stalk package along a finite constants layer
-- statement:
--   Setting. Let $k_0$, $L$, $F$ be fields with $L$ an algebra over $k_0$ and $F$ an algebra over $L$, $L$ of characteristic zero and algebraically closed, and `IsCurveOver L F`, i.e. every nonzero $f\in F$ has a divisor of degree $0$ supported by the orders $\operatorname{ord}_v f$ at the places $v$ of $F/L$, every place has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$; here a place of $F/L$ is a valuation subring of $F$, distinct from $F$, containing the image of $L$ and a principal ideal ring. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $L$ with residue field $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, let $\bar F$ be a field over $\kappa$, let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with values in $\bar F$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ together with a surjective ring map `R.residue` to $\bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, whose contraction to $L$ is $A$, which is compatible with $\kappa\to\bar F$ on $A$, and such that every nonzero $f\in F$ can be scaled by some $c\in L$ into `R.integers` with nonzero residue), and let $Q$ be a place of $\bar F/\kappa$.
--
--   Constants layers. Let $K_1\le K_2$ be intermediate fields of $L/k_0$ (`hK`), with every element of $L$ algebraic over $K_1$ (`halg`) and $K_2$ finite-dimensional over $k_0$ (`hKfin₂`). Let $A_1$, $A_2$ be valuation subrings of $K_1$, $K_2$ cut out by $A$, in the sense that an element belongs to $A_i$ exactly when its image in $L$ belongs to $A$ (`hA₁`, `hA₂`); assume the induced maps $A_i\to\kappa$ sending $a$ to the residue class of its image in $A$ are surjective (`hκ₁`, `hκ₂`), that $A_1$ and $A_2$ are discrete valuation rings (`hdvr₁`, `hdvr₂`) and henselian local rings (`hhens₁`, `hhens₂`), and let $\varpi_2\in A_2$ be a nonzero generator of the maximal ideal of $A_2$ (`hϖ₂`, `hϖ₂0`).
--
--   Layer-one package. Let $S_1$ be a subring of $F$, $\varphi_1:A_1[X]\to S_1$ a ring map, $\chi_1:S_1\to\kappa$ a ring map, and $D_1$ a set of places of $F/L$, subject to the following hypotheses. Chart clauses: the image of $A_1$ in $F$ lies in $S_1$ (`hAS`); $\varphi_1$ is formally smooth and formally unramified (`hφs`, `hφu`); $\varphi_1(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$ (`hφC`); $\chi_1(\varphi_1(C\,a))$ is the residue class of $a$ in $\kappa$ (`hχC`); $\chi_1(\varphi_1 X)=0$ (`hχt`); $\varphi_1 X\ne\varphi_1(C\,c)$ for every $c\in A_1$ (`ht`). Section clauses: for every $c\in A_1$ whose residue class in $\kappa$ vanishes there is a unique ring map $\chi:S_1\to A_1$ with $\chi(\varphi_1(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A_1$, with residue class of $\chi f$ in $\kappa$ equal to $\chi_1 f$ for all $f\in S_1$, and with $\chi(\varphi_1 X)=c$ (`hchart`); and every ring map $\chi:S_1\to A_1$ satisfying the first two of these conditions has kernel generated by $\varphi_1 X-\varphi_1(C\,\chi(\varphi_1 X))$ (`hker`). Prolongation clauses: every $f\in S_1$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the $Q$-residue class of that element is the image of $\chi_1 f$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ (`hres`); and $\varphi_1 X$ lies in `R.integers` with $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of its $R$-residue equal to $1$ (`hordQ`). Disc clause (`hD`): a place $P$ of $F/L$ belongs to $D_1$ if and only if $P$ is rational (the map $L\to P.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), every $f\in S_1$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and for every $f\in S_1$ one has $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ less than $1$ precisely when $\chi_1 f=0$. Algebraic clauses: $S_1$ is local with maximal ideal the kernel of $\chi_1$ (`hlocal`, `hmax`), Noetherian (`hnoeth`) and a unique factorisation monoid (`hufd`); $\varpi\in A_1$ is a nonzero generator of the maximal ideal of $A_1$ (`hϖ`, `hϖ0`) and $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_1$ (`hprime`); for every prime $p$ of $S_1$ not associated to $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x\in S_1$ there is a monic $r\in A_1[X]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of the image of $r$ under $\varphi_1\circ C$ (`hbranch`); and there is a finite subset $G\subseteq S_1$ such that every $f\in S_1$ satisfies $fh=g$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_1$ in $F$ and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_1$ (`hfg`).
--
--   Ambient fields. $F$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\to L\to F$. The assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ such that the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $L$ together with $F_0$ is all of $F$ (`hgen`); writing $F_1$ for the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$ together with $F_0$, it is assumed that $S_1\subseteq F_1$ (`hS₁F₁`), that every $f\in F_1$ satisfies $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in S_1$ with $h\ne 0$ (`hfrac`), that $F_1$ is linearly disjoint from $L$ over $K_1$ in the form: for all $m$, all $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to L$ linearly independent over $K_1$ and all $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to F$ with values in $F_1$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$ (`hld`), and that for $f\in F_1$ one has $f\in$ `R.integers` if and only if $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in S_1$ with $\varphi_1(C\,\varpi)\nmid h$ (`hRint`).
--
--   Conclusion. There exist a subring $S_2$ of $F$, a ring map $\varphi_2:A_2[X]\to S_2$ and a ring map $\chi_2:S_2\to\kappa$ such that, writing $F_2$ for the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K_2$ together with $F_0$:
--
--   (i) $S_1\le S_2$, and $S_2$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_1$ together with the image of $A_2$ in $F$; the two parameters agree in $F$, $\varphi_1 X=\varphi_2 X$; and $\chi_2$ restricted to $S_1$ is $\chi_1$.
--
--   (ii) The image of $A_2$ in $F$ lies in $S_2$. (iii) $\varphi_2$ is formally smooth and formally unramified. (iv) $\varphi_2(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$ for every $a\in A_2$. (v) $\chi_2(\varphi_2(C\,a))$ is the residue class of $a$ in $\kappa$. (vi) $\chi_2(\varphi_2 X)=0$.
--
--   (vii) For every $c\in A_2$ with vanishing residue class in $\kappa$ there is a unique ring map $\chi:S_2\to A_2$ with $\chi(\varphi_2(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A_2$, with residue class of $\chi f$ equal to $\chi_2 f$ for all $f\in S_2$, and with $\chi(\varphi_2 X)=c$.
--
--   (viii) Every $f\in S_2$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the $Q$-residue class of that element is the image of $\chi_2 f$ in $Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$. (ix) $\varphi_2 X$ lies in `R.integers` and $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of its $R$-residue equals $1$.
--
--   (x) The same set $D_1$ is described by the new data: a place $P$ lies in $D_1$ if and only if $P$ is rational, every $f\in S_2$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and for every $f\in S_2$ the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is less than $1$ precisely when $\chi_2 f=0$.
--
--   (xi) $\varphi_2 X\ne\varphi_2(C\,c)$ for every $c\in A_2$. (xii) $S_2$ is local with maximal ideal the kernel of $\chi_2$. (xiii) $S_2$ is Noetherian and a unique factorisation monoid. (xiv) $S_2\subseteq F_2$. (xv) Every $f\in F_2$ satisfies $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in S_2$ with $h\ne0$. (xvi) $\varphi_2(C\,\varpi_2)$ is prime in $S_2$. (xvii) For $f\in F_2$ one has $f\in$ `R.integers` if and only if $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in S_2$ with $\varphi_2(C\,\varpi_2)\nmid h$.
--
--   (xviii) Every ring map $\chi:S_2\to A_2$ that is an $A_2$-section ($\chi(\varphi_2(C\,a))=a$) and lifts $\chi_2$ (residue class of $\chi f$ equals $\chi_2 f$) has kernel generated by $\varphi_2 X-\varphi_2(C\,\chi(\varphi_2 X))$. (xix) For every prime $p$ of $S_2$ not associated to $\varphi_2(C\,\varpi_2)$ and every $x\in S_2$ there is a monic $r\in A_2[X]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of the image of $r$ under $\varphi_2\circ C$. (xx) There is a finite subset $G\subseteq S_2$ such that every $f\in S_2$ satisfies $fh=g$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_2$ in $F$, and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_2$.
--
--   Thus the conclusion reproduces, over $A_2$ and $F_2$, every clause of the layer-one hypothesis list except the linear-disjointness clause `hld`, for which no analogue over $K_2$ is asserted, and it adds the compatibility bundle (i).
--
--   This is the one-layer base-change step in the construction of a tower of smooth-point stalk packages on a curve over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero: from a package $(S_1,\varphi_1,\chi_1,D_1)$ over a layer of constants $K_1$ it produces a package over a finite layer $K_2$ with the same local parameter and compatible residue character. It is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_smoothPointStalks_tower_of_base`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_smoothPointStalks_tower_of_base) and, through it, by the full-level modular-curve statements that supply smooth-point packages, node presentations and charts at supersingular points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_RegularProlongation_exists_smoothPointStalk_baseChange_layer.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_ResidueDiscs
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open AlgebraicCurve IsLocalRing

theorem AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_smoothPointStalk_baseChange_layer
    {k₀ L F : Type} [Field k₀] [Field L] [Field F] [Algebra k₀ L] [Algebra L F]
    [CharZero L] [IsAlgClosed L] [IsCurveOver L F]
    (A : ValuationSubring L)
    {Fbar : Type} [Field Fbar] [Algebra (ResidueField ↥A) Fbar]
    (R : RegularProlongation A F Fbar) (Q : Place (ResidueField ↥A) Fbar)

    (K₁ K₂ : IntermediateField k₀ L) (hK : K₁ ≤ K₂) (halg : ∀ x : L, IsAlgebraic ↥K₁ x)
    (hKfin₂ : FiniteDimensional k₀ ↥K₂)
    (A₁ : ValuationSubring ↥K₁) (hA₁ : ∀ x : ↥K₁, x ∈ A₁ ↔ (x : L) ∈ A)
    (A₂ : ValuationSubring ↥K₂) (hA₂ : ∀ x : ↥K₂, x ∈ A₂ ↔ (x : L) ∈ A)
    (hκ₁ : Function.Surjective (fun a : ↥A₁ => IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((a : ↥K₁) : L), (hA₁ a).mp a.2⟩))
    (hκ₂ : Function.Surjective (fun a : ↥A₂ => IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((a : ↥K₂) : L), (hA₂ a).mp a.2⟩))
    (hdvr₁ : IsDiscreteValuationRing ↥A₁) (hdvr₂ : IsDiscreteValuationRing ↥A₂)
    (hhens₁ : HenselianLocalRing ↥A₁) (hhens₂ : HenselianLocalRing ↥A₂)
    (ϖ₂ : ↥A₂) (hϖ₂ : maximalIdeal ↥A₂ = Ideal.span {ϖ₂}) (hϖ₂0 : ϖ₂ ≠ 0)

    (S₁ : Subring F) (φ₁ : Polynomial ↥A₁ →+* ↥S₁) (χ₁ : ↥S₁ →+* ResidueField ↥A) (D₁ : Set (Place L F))
    (hAS : ∀ a : ↥A₁, algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₁) : L) ∈ S₁)
    (hφs : φ₁.FormallySmooth) (hφu : φ₁.FormallyUnramified)
    (hφC : ∀ a : ↥A₁, ((φ₁ (Polynomial.C a) : ↥S₁) : F) = algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₁) : L))
    (hχC : ∀ a : ↥A₁, χ₁ (φ₁ (Polynomial.C a)) = IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((a : ↥K₁) : L), (hA₁ a).mp a.2⟩)
    (hχt : χ₁ (φ₁ Polynomial.X) = 0)
    (hchart : ∀ c : ↥A₁, IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((c : ↥K₁) : L), (hA₁ c).mp c.2⟩ = 0 →
      ∃! χ : ↥S₁ →+* ↥A₁, (∀ a : ↥A₁, χ (φ₁ (Polynomial.C a)) = a) ∧
        (∀ f : ↥S₁, IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((χ f : ↥K₁) : L), (hA₁ _).mp (χ f).2⟩ = χ₁ f) ∧ χ (φ₁ Polynomial.X) = c)
    (hker : ∀ χ : ↥S₁ →+* ↥A₁, (∀ a : ↥A₁, χ (φ₁ (Polynomial.C a)) = a) →
      (∀ f : ↥S₁, IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((χ f : ↥K₁) : L), (hA₁ _).mp (χ f).2⟩ = χ₁ f) →
      RingHom.ker χ = Ideal.span {φ₁ Polynomial.X - φ₁ (Polynomial.C (χ (φ₁ Polynomial.X)))})
    (hres : ∀ f : ↥S₁, ∃ hR : (f : F) ∈ R.integers, ∃ hm : R.residue ⟨(f : F), hR⟩ ∈ Q.toValuationSubring,
      IsLocalRing.residue ↥Q.toValuationSubring ⟨R.residue ⟨(f : F), hR⟩, hm⟩ =
        algebraMap (ResidueField ↥A) Q.ResidueField (χ₁ f))
    (hordQ : ∃ hR : ((φ₁ Polynomial.X : ↥S₁) : F) ∈ R.integers,
      Q.ord (R.residue ⟨((φ₁ Polynomial.X : ↥S₁) : F), hR⟩) = 1)
    (hD : ∀ P, P ∈ D₁ ↔ (P.IsRational ∧
      (∀ f : ↥S₁, (f : F) ∈ P.toValuationSubring ∧ P.evalAt (f : F) ∈ A) ∧
      (∀ f : ↥S₁, A.valuation (P.evalAt (f : F)) < 1 ↔ χ₁ f = 0)))
    (ht : ∀ c : ↥A₁, φ₁ Polynomial.X ≠ φ₁ (Polynomial.C c))
    (hlocal : IsLocalRing ↥S₁) (hmax : ∀ f : ↥S₁, f ∈ maximalIdeal ↥S₁ ↔ χ₁ f = 0)
    (hnoeth : IsNoetherianRing ↥S₁) (hufd : UniqueFactorizationMonoid ↥S₁)
    (ϖ : ↥A₁) (hϖ : maximalIdeal ↥A₁ = Ideal.span {ϖ}) (hϖ0 : ϖ ≠ 0)
    (hprime : Prime (φ₁ (Polynomial.C ϖ)))
    (hbranch : ∀ p : ↥S₁, Prime p → ¬ Associated p (φ₁ (Polynomial.C ϖ)) →
      ∀ x : ↥S₁, ∃ r : Polynomial ↥A₁, r.Monic ∧ p ∣ (r.map (φ₁.comp Polynomial.C)).eval x)
    (hfg : ∃ G : Finset F, ↑G ⊆ (S₁ : Set F) ∧ ∀ f ∈ S₁, ∃ g h : F,
      g ∈ Subring.closure (↑G ∪ ((fun a : ↥A₁ => algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₁) : L)) '' Set.univ)) ∧
      h ∈ Subring.closure (↑G ∪ ((fun a : ↥A₁ => algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₁) : L)) '' Set.univ)) ∧
      (∃ u : (↥S₁)ˣ, ((u : ↥S₁) : F) = h) ∧ f * h = g) :
    letI : Algebra k₀ F := ((algebraMap L F).comp (algebraMap k₀ L)).toAlgebra
    ∀ (F₀ : IntermediateField k₀ F)
      (hgen : IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap L F)) ⊔ F₀ = ⊤)
      (hS₁F₁ : ∀ f : F, f ∈ S₁ → f ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (⇑(algebraMap L F) '' (↑K₁ : Set L)) ⊔ F₀)
      (hfrac : ∀ f : F, f ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (⇑(algebraMap L F) '' (↑K₁ : Set L)) ⊔ F₀ → ∃ g h : ↥S₁, (h : F) ≠ 0 ∧ f * (h : F) = (g : F))
      (hld : ∀ (m : ℕ) (c : Fin m → L) (a : Fin m → F), (∀ i, a i ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (⇑(algebraMap L F) '' (↑K₁ : Set L)) ⊔ F₀) →
        LinearIndependent ↥K₁ c → ∑ i, algebraMap L F (c i) * a i = 0 → ∀ i, a i = 0)
      (hRint : ∀ f : F, f ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (⇑(algebraMap L F) '' (↑K₁ : Set L)) ⊔ F₀ →
        (f ∈ R.integers ↔ ∃ g h : ↥S₁, ¬ (φ₁ (Polynomial.C ϖ) ∣ h) ∧ f * (h : F) = (g : F))),
    ∃ (S₂ : Subring F) (φ₂ : Polynomial ↥A₂ →+* ↥S₂) (χ₂ : ↥S₂ →+* ResidueField ↥A),

      (∃ hmono : S₁ ≤ S₂,
        S₂ ≤ Subring.closure ((S₁ : Set F) ∪ ((fun a : ↥A₂ => algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₂) : L)) '' Set.univ)) ∧
        ((φ₁ Polynomial.X : ↥S₁) : F) = ((φ₂ Polynomial.X : ↥S₂) : F) ∧
        (∀ f : ↥S₁, χ₂ ⟨(f : F), hmono f.2⟩ = χ₁ f)) ∧

      (∀ a : ↥A₂, algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₂) : L) ∈ S₂) ∧
      φ₂.FormallySmooth ∧ φ₂.FormallyUnramified ∧
      (∀ a : ↥A₂, ((φ₂ (Polynomial.C a) : ↥S₂) : F) = algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₂) : L)) ∧
      (∀ a : ↥A₂, χ₂ (φ₂ (Polynomial.C a)) = IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((a : ↥K₂) : L), (hA₂ a).mp a.2⟩) ∧
      χ₂ (φ₂ Polynomial.X) = 0 ∧
      (∀ c : ↥A₂, IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((c : ↥K₂) : L), (hA₂ c).mp c.2⟩ = 0 →
        ∃! χ : ↥S₂ →+* ↥A₂, (∀ a : ↥A₂, χ (φ₂ (Polynomial.C a)) = a) ∧
          (∀ f : ↥S₂, IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((χ f : ↥K₂) : L), (hA₂ _).mp (χ f).2⟩ = χ₂ f) ∧ χ (φ₂ Polynomial.X) = c) ∧
      (∀ f : ↥S₂, ∃ hR : (f : F) ∈ R.integers, ∃ hm : R.residue ⟨(f : F), hR⟩ ∈ Q.toValuationSubring,
        IsLocalRing.residue ↥Q.toValuationSubring ⟨R.residue ⟨(f : F), hR⟩, hm⟩ =
          algebraMap (ResidueField ↥A) Q.ResidueField (χ₂ f)) ∧
      (∃ hR : ((φ₂ Polynomial.X : ↥S₂) : F) ∈ R.integers,
        Q.ord (R.residue ⟨((φ₂ Polynomial.X : ↥S₂) : F), hR⟩) = 1) ∧
      (∀ P, P ∈ D₁ ↔ (P.IsRational ∧
        (∀ f : ↥S₂, (f : F) ∈ P.toValuationSubring ∧ P.evalAt (f : F) ∈ A) ∧
        (∀ f : ↥S₂, A.valuation (P.evalAt (f : F)) < 1 ↔ χ₂ f = 0))) ∧
      (∀ c : ↥A₂, φ₂ Polynomial.X ≠ φ₂ (Polynomial.C c)) ∧
      (∃ _ : IsLocalRing ↥S₂, ∀ f : ↥S₂, f ∈ maximalIdeal ↥S₂ ↔ χ₂ f = 0) ∧
      IsNoetherianRing ↥S₂ ∧ UniqueFactorizationMonoid ↥S₂ ∧
      (∀ f : F, f ∈ S₂ → f ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (⇑(algebraMap L F) '' (↑K₂ : Set L)) ⊔ F₀) ∧
      (∀ f : F, f ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (⇑(algebraMap L F) '' (↑K₂ : Set L)) ⊔ F₀ → ∃ g h : ↥S₂, (h : F) ≠ 0 ∧ f * (h : F) = (g : F)) ∧
      Prime (φ₂ (Polynomial.C ϖ₂)) ∧
      (∀ f : F, f ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (⇑(algebraMap L F) '' (↑K₂ : Set L)) ⊔ F₀ →
        (f ∈ R.integers ↔ ∃ g h : ↥S₂, ¬ (φ₂ (Polynomial.C ϖ₂) ∣ h) ∧ f * (h : F) = (g : F))) ∧
      (∀ χ : ↥S₂ →+* ↥A₂, (∀ a : ↥A₂, χ (φ₂ (Polynomial.C a)) = a) →
        (∀ f : ↥S₂, IsLocalRing.residue ↥A ⟨((χ f : ↥K₂) : L), (hA₂ _).mp (χ f).2⟩ = χ₂ f) →
        RingHom.ker χ = Ideal.span {φ₂ Polynomial.X - φ₂ (Polynomial.C (χ (φ₂ Polynomial.X)))}) ∧
      (∀ p : ↥S₂, Prime p → ¬ Associated p (φ₂ (Polynomial.C ϖ₂)) →
        ∀ x : ↥S₂, ∃ r : Polynomial ↥A₂, r.Monic ∧ p ∣ (r.map (φ₂.comp Polynomial.C)).eval x) ∧
      (∃ G : Finset F, ↑G ⊆ (S₂ : Set F) ∧ ∀ f ∈ S₂, ∃ g h : F,
        g ∈ Subring.closure (↑G ∪ ((fun a : ↥A₂ => algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₂) : L)) '' Set.univ)) ∧
        h ∈ Subring.closure (↑G ∪ ((fun a : ↥A₂ => algebraMap L F ((a : ↥K₂) : L)) '' Set.univ)) ∧
        (∃ u : (↥S₂)ˣ, ((u : ↥S₂) : F) = h) ∧ f * h = g) := by sorry
